---
template: recipe
title: Pancakes for a cold morning
subtitle: Thick, soft, and quick enough to make before anyone else is awake.
serves: 4
time: 25 minutes
---

:::steps
### Make the batter
Whisk :ingredient[plain flour](qty=200, unit=g), :ingredient[caster sugar](qty=1, unit=tbsp),
:ingredient[baking powder](qty=2, unit=tsp) and :ingredient[salt](qty=1, unit=pinch) in a big bowl.

### Bring it together
Beat :ingredient[eggs](qty=2) into :ingredient[milk](qty=300, unit=ml) with
:ingredient[butter](qty=30, unit=g), melted. Pour it into the flour and stir until _just_
combined. Lumps are fine; a smooth batter is a tough pancake.

### Rest
Leave it for ten minutes, while the pan heats. Go and wake someone.

### Cook
Melt a little more :ingredient[butter](qty=10, unit=g) in the pan. A ladle of batter at a
time, two minutes a side, until bubbles break on top and the edges set.

### Serve
Stack them high, with :ingredient[maple syrup](qty=4, unit=tbsp) and
:ingredient[blueberries](qty=150, unit=g).
:::
